      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An SRO-induced rise in SFE increases the energy barrier for dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower-temperature or sub-critical annealing can induce local chemical order or SRO in concentrated alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6687833::page::002",
        "PMC9645729::page::002"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sub-critical annealing can vary SRO without causing phase decomposition.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At lower temperatures, enthalpic solute interactions become more important than configurational entropy and promote local chemical ordering.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6687833::page::002",
        "PMC9645729::page::002"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
